<title>POLAND: POLISH CROPS RATINGS FLAT IN AUGUST 1-10.</title>
<headline>POLISH CROPS RATINGS FLAT IN AUGUST 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Meteorology and Water</p>
<p>Management Institute (IMGW) on Wednesday said crop conditions</p>
<p>in August 1-10 were mostly unchanged from the previous 10 days</p>
<p>and remained slightly below corresponding 1996 levels.</p>
<p>Ratings are made three times a month based on the condition</p>
<p>and development of crops on a scale of one to five, with five</p>
<p>being the highest grade.</p>
<p> POLISH CROP RATINGS    AUG 10   JULY 31  1996   5-YR AVG</p>
<p> Wheat (spring)	    3.4	 3.4     3.6	N/A</p>
<p> Barley (spring)	   3.4	 3.4     3.5	N/A</p>
<p> Oats			  3.3	 3.3     3.5	N/A</p>
<p> Sugar beets		 3.7	 3.7     3.8	3.1</p>
<p> Potatoes		    3.0	 3.2     3.6	3.0</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
